  If these spreads are LARGE, per-hour solutions exist and gradient descent
  finds them -- the collapse is then the OUTER average over windows, i.e. the
  deployed policy is a barycenter of the phi_h.
  If they are SMALL, the collapse happens inside one window and the outer
  average is not the cause.

